{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:45:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T14:15:30+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T14:15:30+05:30\nThe following changes were made by the replace_file_content tool to: c:\\Abhi\\AntiGravity\\DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11\\DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11\\start_server.bat. If relevant, proactively run terminal commands to execute this code for the USER. Don't ask for permission.\n[diff_block_start]\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n @echo off\n setlocal\n cd /d \"%~dp0\"\n-if \"%DATABASE_URL%\"==\"\" set DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///clinic_local.db\n+if \"%DATABASE_URL%\"==\"\" set DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/clinic_erp\n \n if exist \".venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" (\n     set \"PY_CMD=.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\"\n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown."}
{"step_index":120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T08:45:30Z","content":"To run the newly unified PostgreSQL-based project, you will need to follow these steps:\n\n### Step 1: Install PostgreSQL\nSince we migrated to use PostgreSQL for both SaaS and Desktop models:\n1. Ensure you have **PostgreSQL** installed and running on your machine.\n2. Open pgAdmin (or your psql terminal) and create an empty database named `clinic_erp`.\n\n### Step 2: Install Python Dependencies\nOpen a PowerShell terminal in the inner project folder and run:\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Abhi\\AntiGravity\\DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11\\DhanvantariSuite-Phase1-Professional-OPD-v11\n\n# This will install FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, and the new Postgres driver (psycopg2-binary)\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### Step 3: Configure Database Credentials (Optional)\nThe system defaults to a local Postgres instance with the user `postgres` and password `postgres`.\nIf your local Postgres password is different, you must set the environment variable before running:\n```powershell\n$env:DATABASE_URL=\"postgresql://your_db_username:your_db_password@localhost:5432/clinic_erp\"\n```\n\n### Step 4: Start the Server\nI have updated your `start_server.bat` file to use PostgreSQL. You can run the server by simply executing it:\n```powershell\n.\\start_server.bat\n```\n\nAlternatively, you can run it directly via Python:\n```powershell\npython -m uvicorn src.main:app --reload --port 8000\n```\n\n### Step 5: Access the Application\nOnce the server starts, it will automatically create all the necessary multi-tenant tables in your PostgreSQL database and seed the initial users.\n- Open your browser and go to: **http://127.0.0.1:8000/ui/**\n- You can log in using any of the seeded demo accounts:\n  - **Admin:** `admin_user` / `adminpass123`\n  - **Receptionist:** `receptionist_user` / `receppass123`\n  - **Doctor:** `doctor_user` / `docpass123`\n\n*(Note: If you run into any connection refused errors in Step 4, it means PostgreSQL isn't running or the password credentials are incorrect!)*"}
